{"atonupasarge kaH": [{"id": "Ato'nupasarge kaH", "headword": "आतोऽनुपसर्गे कः", "headword_slp1": "Ato'nupasarge kaH", "fold": "atonupasarge kaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix क comes after a verbal root that ends in long आ when there is no उपसर्ग preceding it and when the object is in composition with it.\n\nTerms: अण्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतोऽनुपसर्गे कः ३.२.३", "३.२.३", "३.२.३ आतोऽनुपसर्गे कः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato'nupasarge kaH ३.२.३", "३.२.३", "३.२.३ Ato'nupasarge kaH"]}], "ato maninkvanipvanipasca": [{"id": "Ato maninkvanipvanipaSca", "headword": "आतो मनिन्क्वनिप्वनिपश्च", "headword_slp1": "Ato maninkvanipvanipaSca", "fold": "ato maninkvanipvanipasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affixes मनिन् (मन्), वनिप् (वन्), विनय (वन्) and विच् come in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the verbs which end in long आ , when used in a case-inflected word or उपसर्ग in in composition. \n\nTerms: छन्दस्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतो मनिन्क्वनिप्वनिपश्च ३.२.७४", "३.२.७४", "३.२.७४ आतो मनिन्क्वनिप्वनिपश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato maninkvanipvanipaSca ३.२.७४", "३.२.७४", "३.२.७४ Ato maninkvanipvanipaSca"]}], "ato yuc": [{"id": "Ato yuc", "headword": "आतो युच्", "headword_slp1": "Ato yuc", "fold": "ato yuc", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix युच् comes after the roots ending in long आ (when ईषद् and दुर् and सु are combined as उपपद-sūtras, in the sense of easily or with difficulty).\n\nTerms: युच्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतो युच् ३.३.१२८", "३.३.१२८", "३.३.१२८ आतो युच्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato yuc ३.३.१२८", "३.३.१२८", "३.३.१२८ Ato yuc"]}], "ato guRe": [{"id": "ato guRe", "headword": "अतो गुणे", "headword_slp1": "ato guRe", "fold": "ato guRe", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Also when the short अ , not being final in a पद , is followed by a गुण letter, then in the room of both the precedent and the subsequent - the single substitute is the form of the subsequent i.e. the गुण।\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो गुणे ६.१.९७", "६.१.९७", "६.१.९७ अतो गुणे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato guRe ६.१.९७", "६.१.९७", "६.१.९७ ato guRe"]}], "ato roraplutadaplute": [{"id": "ato roraplutAdaplute", "headword": "अतो रोरप्लुतादप्लुते", "headword_slp1": "ato roraplutAdaplute", "fold": "ato roraplutadaplute", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The उ is the substitute of रु (the र् substitute of a final स् ८.२.६६) when an अ , which is not a प्लुत, both precedes and follows it.\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो रोरप्लुतादप्लुते ६.१.११३", "६.१.११३", "६.१.११३ अतो रोरप्लुतादप्लुते"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato roraplutAdaplute ६.१.११३", "६.१.११३", "६.१.११३ ato roraplutAdaplute"]}], "ato lopaH": [{"id": "ato lopaH", "headword": "अतो लोपः", "headword_slp1": "ato lopaH", "fold": "ato lopaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The अ standing at the end of a अङ्ग (stem) is elided before an आर्धधातुक affix.\n\nTerms: आर्धधातुक changes", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो लोपः ६.४.४८", "६.४.४८", "६.४.४८ अतो लोपः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato lopaH ६.४.४८", "६.४.४८", "६.४.४८ ato lopaH"]}], "ato lopa iwi ca": [{"id": "Ato lopa iwi ca", "headword": "आतो लोप इटि च", "headword_slp1": "Ato lopa iwi ca", "fold": "ato lopa iwi ca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The final आ of a root is elided before an आर्धधातुक affix with the augment इट् as well as when it begins with a vowel and has an indicatory क् or ङ्।\n\nTerms: आर्धधातुक changes", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतो लोप इटि च ६.४.६४", "६.४.६४", "६.४.६४ आतो लोप इटि च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato lopa iwi ca ६.४.६४", "६.४.६४", "६.४.६४ Ato lopa iwi ca"]}], "ato heH": [{"id": "ato heH", "headword": "अतो हेः", "headword_slp1": "ato heH", "fold": "ato heH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The Imperative affix हि is elided after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in short अ।\n\nTerms: कित् and ङित्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो हेः ६.४.१०५", "६.४.१०५", "६.४.१०५ अतो हेः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato heH ६.४.१०५", "६.४.१०५", "६.४.१०५ ato heH"]}], "ato DatoH": [{"id": "Ato DAtoH", "headword": "आतो धातोः", "headword_slp1": "Ato DAtoH", "fold": "ato DatoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The final आ of a भ अङ्ग (stem) is elided when it ends in a root.\n\nTerms: आ elision", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतो धातोः ६.४.१४०", "६.४.१४०", "६.४.१४० आतो धातोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato DAtoH ६.४.१४०", "६.४.१४०", "६.४.१४० Ato DAtoH"]}], "ato Bisa Es": [{"id": "ato Bisa Es", "headword": "अतो भिस ऐस्", "headword_slp1": "ato Bisa Es", "fold": "ato Bisa Es", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After a nominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ, ऐस् is substituted for the case-ending भिस्।\n\nTerms: Some substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो भिस ऐस् ७.१.९", "७.१.९", "७.१.९ अतो भिस ऐस्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato Bisa Es ७.१.९", "७.१.९", "७.१.९ ato Bisa Es"]}], "atom": [{"id": "ato'm", "headword": "अतोऽम्", "headword_slp1": "ato'm", "fold": "atom", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After a neutral अङ्ग (stem) अ , अम् is substituted for सु and अम् , the Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case endings.\n\nTerms: Some substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतोऽम् ७.१.२४", "७.१.२४", "७.१.२४ अतोऽम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato'm ७.१.२४", "७.१.२४", "७.१.२४ ato'm"]}], "ato rlantasya": [{"id": "ato rlAntasya", "headword": "अतो र्लान्तस्य", "headword_slp1": "ato rlAntasya", "fold": "ato rlantasya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "वृद्धि is substituted for the short अ when it is immediately followed by the final र् or ल् of a root, before the परस्मैपद s-Aorist.\n\nTerms: Aorist वृद्धि", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो र्लान्तस्य ७.२.२", "७.२.२", "७.२.२ अतो र्लान्तस्य"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato rlAntasya ७.२.२", "७.२.२", "७.२.२ ato rlAntasya"]}], "ato haladerlaGoH": [{"id": "ato halAderlaGoH", "headword": "अतो हलादेर्लघोः", "headword_slp1": "ato halAderlaGoH", "fold": "ato haladerlaGoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Before the इट् beginning s-Aorist of the परस्मैपद the short अ of the root gets optionally वृद्धि when the अङ्ग (stem) begins with a consonant and the अ is prosodially short by being followed by a simple consonant.\n\nTerms: Aorist वृद्धि", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो हलादेर्लघोः ७.२.७", "७.२.७", "७.२.७ अतो हलादेर्लघोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato halAderlaGoH ७.२.७", "७.२.७", "७.२.७ ato halAderlaGoH"]}], "ato yeyaH": [{"id": "ato yeyaH", "headword": "अतो येयः", "headword_slp1": "ato yeyaH", "fold": "ato yeyaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After a Present अङ्ग (stem) ending in a short अ , इय् is substituted for the सार्वधातुक या (i.e. for the या of the augment यास् of the लिङ् (Potential)).\n\nTerms: Some substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो येयः ७.२.८०", "७.२.८०", "७.२.८० अतो येयः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato yeyaH ७.२.८०", "७.२.८०", "७.२.८० ato yeyaH"]}], "ato NitaH": [{"id": "Ato NitaH", "headword": "आतो ङितः", "headword_slp1": "Ato NitaH", "fold": "ato NitaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "For the आ being a portion of a सार्वधातुक personal-ending which is ङित् (i.e. आते , आथे and आताम् and आथाम्), coming after a verbal अङ्ग (stem) ending in a short अ , there is substituted इय् ।\n\nTerms: Some substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतो ङितः ७.२.८१", "७.२.८१", "७.२.८१ आतो ङितः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato NitaH ७.२.८१", "७.२.८१", "७.२.८१ Ato NitaH"]}], "ato yuk ciRkftoH": [{"id": "Ato yuk ciRkftoH", "headword": "आतो युक् चिण्कृतोः", "headword_slp1": "Ato yuk ciRkftoH", "fold": "ato yuk ciRkftoH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A root-अङ्ग (stem) ending in आ gets the augment युक् (य्) before the Aorist sign चिण् which causes also the वृद्धि of the root-vowel.\n\nTerms: वृद्धि", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतो युक् चिण्कृतोः ७.३.३३", "७.३.३३", "७.३.३३ आतो युक् चिण्कृतोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato yuk ciRkftoH ७.३.३३", "७.३.३३", "७.३.३३ Ato yuk ciRkftoH"]}], "ato dirGo yaYi": [{"id": "ato dIrGo yaYi", "headword": "अतो दीर्घो यञि", "headword_slp1": "ato dIrGo yaYi", "fold": "ato dirGo yaYi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The long आ is substituted for the final अ of a tense अङ्ग (stem) before a सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a व् or म् (literally a consonant of यञ् प्रत्यहार).\n\nTerms: Lengthening", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["अतो दीर्घो यञि ७.३.१०१", "७.३.१०१", "७.३.१०१ अतो दीर्घो यञि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["ato dIrGo yaYi ७.३.१०१", "७.३.१०१", "७.३.१०१ ato dIrGo yaYi"]}], "atowi nityam": [{"id": "Ato'wi nityam", "headword": "आतोऽटि नित्यम्", "headword_slp1": "Ato'wi nityam", "fold": "atowi nityam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "A nasal vowel is ALWAYS substituted for आ before रु when it is followed by a letter of अट् प्रत्यहार (i.e. when it is followed by a vowel or ह , य , व or र).\n\nTerms: Nasal रु", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["आतोऽटि नित्यम् ८.३.३", "८.३.३", "८.३.३ आतोऽटि नित्यम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["Ato'wi nityam ८.३.३", "८.३.३", "८.३.३ Ato'wi nityam"]}]}